From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 02:18:26 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] irqchip/apple-aic: Save and restore AICv3 state
 across system sleep too

The AICv2 save/restore added for suspend-to-RAM only registers for
version 2. AICv3 (T8122, T8132) uses the same register layout, starting
at AIC3_IRQ_CFG, with CONFIG at the AICv2 offset (the driver already
enables both versions through AIC2_CONFIG), and goes through the same
SoC power-down in suspend-to-RAM. Register the same syscore hooks for it.

Without this, a T8132 suspend-to-RAM would come back with every AIC
interrupt masked and unconfigured.

The syscore hooks only run for platform suspend (mem) and hibernation;
suspend-to-idle is unchanged.

Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/irqchip/irq-apple-aic.c | 5 +++--
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/irqchip/irq-apple-aic.c b/drivers/irqchip/irq-apple-aic.c
index 2272334f21..152f9cc987 100644
--- a/drivers/irqchip/irq-apple-aic.c
+++ b/drivers/irqchip/irq-apple-aic.c
@@ -1052,7 +1052,7 @@ static int aic_init_cpu(unsigned int cpu)
 
 #ifdef CONFIG_PM_SLEEP
 /*
- * AICv2 loses CONFIG, IRQ_CFG and the mask bits when the SoC enters
+ * AICv2 and AICv3 lose CONFIG, IRQ_CFG and the mask bits when the SoC enters
  * suspend-to-RAM. Save them and mask every interrupt on the way down; restore
  * them before interrupts are re-enabled on the way up.
  */
@@ -1313,7 +1313,8 @@ static int __init aic_of_ic_init(struct device_node *node, struct device_node *p
 		aic_ic_write(irqc, AIC2_CONFIG, config);
 	}
 
-	if (irqc->info.version == 2)
+	/* AICv3 keeps the AICv2 layout from AIC3_IRQ_CFG and loses it too */
+	if (irqc->info.version == 2 || irqc->info.version == 3)
 		aic2_init_pm(irqc);
 
 	if (!is_kernel_in_hyp_mode())
